<BaseLayout title="Phase 2 -- Off-the-shelf replacement for Myriad">

  <h1 class="page-title">Phase 2</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">Buy an off-the-shelf replacement for Myriad <span class="verdict rejected">Not affordable</span></p>
  <p class="phase-meta">May 2023 to June 2024</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">Hypothesis</h2>
  <p>Could we buy an off-the-shelf software solution to completely replace Myriad and modernise subscription management in one step?</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">What we explored</h2>
  <p>We conducted a light-touch market research exercise, benchmarking five alternative software vendors -- including Pelcro, Affino, AdvantageCS, and ChargeBee -- and obtaining quotes. We also ran cross-departmental SWOT analyses on Myriad and interviewed other publishers about their experiences with alternative systems.</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">What we found</h2>
  <p>Every alternative system evaluated was significantly more expensive than Myriad. Internal teams had mixed feelings: Customer Service valued Myriad's rigid controls, while Client Management found it clunky and limiting.</p>
  <p>Most critically, we discovered that our bespoke external systems were so tightly coupled to Myriad that a direct "lift and shift" migration was impossible. A direct replacement would require unpicking years of custom integrations before any new system could be brought in.</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">Decision and reasoning</h2>
  <p>We decided not to migrate to a new system immediately. Before any replacement could be viable, we needed to "detangle" our custom systems from Myriad by building a middle integration layer. This would allow ESco to integrate payment processing and eCommerce out of the box in the future, and make any future CRM swap far more straightforward.</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">Key supporting documents</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>Tech Transformation Phase 2 Report v1.pdf</li>
    <li>2024_06_13_FindingsWithNotes.pdf</li>
    <li>2023_05_11_Phase 2 Kick Off v1.pdf</li>
  </ul>

